{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795673117,"nonce":"/CZOXI/BkPNIpLg4xCY7wXGE+jE=","title":"Let AWS trust Scarab-issued OIDC tokens per step (sub = repo/env/ref), replacing the broad IRSA roles every Treebo step Pod shares today. Status: design only, to be discussed with the owner. Nothing is configured on the Treebo instance or in AWS.","message":"The owner called it \"the oidc work pending for the service accounts\". The account below comes\nfrom the Treebo devops-gitops work (2026-11-26); before this ticket there was no issue, ADR or\nplan.\n\n**Recorded** (the owner's decision of 2026-11-24): while porting the dwh pipelines,\nnarrow per-pipeline AWS roles were proposed. The owner chose Woodpecker parity instead: every\nScarab step gets one broad shared role. Narrowing was deferred to \"Scarab OIDC federation\n(sub = repo/env/ref, AWS-enforced)\" as a separate plan.\n\n**Inference** (to confirm with the owner): \"the service accounts\" means the two\nKubernetes ServiceAccounts step Pods use today through IRSA (EKS's own OIDC), in namespace\n`scarab-steps`:\n- `scarab-steps`: Woodpecker's step rights (`tools/woodpecker/policy.json` in devops-gitops)\n  plus permission to assume the read-only Terraform plan role. Every step gets this.\n- `scarab-ecr-push`: the `registry_auth_only` ecr-push profile; only its `ecr-login` init\n  container gets the role.\n\nBoth are bound per Pod, not per repo, Environment or ref, so any step in any repo gets the same\nAWS rights. The work: AWS trusts *Scarab* as an OIDC provider and each role's trust policy\nmatches the token's `sub`. For example, only `treebo-noss/dwh` in env `production` may assume\nthe production SSM role, and only `devops-gitops` may assume the Terraform plan role.\n\nIt is **outbound** workload identity (Scarab → AWS STS `AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity`). It is not\nScarab service-account principals, and it is unrelated to the MCP server (9130efd).\n\n\n- **The issuer** (ADR-0015, `docs/adr/0015-supply-chain-oidc.md`): `crates/scarab-server/src/oidc.rs`.\n  RS256. Enabled by `SCARAB_OIDC_ISSUER` (chart value `scarab.oidcIssuer`), with\n  `SCARAB_OIDC_SIGNING_KEY_FILE` (persistent PKCS#8 RSA PEM; the server refuses to boot without\n  one) and `SCARAB_OIDC_AUDIENCE` (default `scarab`, one value server-wide). See\n  `crates/scarab-server/src/config.rs` ~42-44 and ~1625.\n- **Discovery and JWKS** are served by scarab-server at `/.well-known/openid-configuration` and\n  `/.well-known/jwks.json` on its own host, and return 404 when the issuer is off\n  (`crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs` ~16623-16630). `jwks_uri` is derived from the issuer URL\n  (`oidc.rs` ~114).\n- **Per-attempt token**: minted in `crates/scarab-server/src/secret_executor.rs` `mint_oidc_token`\n  (~693-740), TTL 15 minutes (~557). It is mounted into the step Pod at `/scarab/oidc/token`\n  (`crates/scarab-executor-k8s/src/lib.rs` ~6963).\n- **Subject**: `scarab:org/\u003corg\u003e/repo/\u003crepo\u003e/env/\u003cenv\u003e/ref/\u003cref\u003e`\n  (`crates/scarab-identity/src/lib.rs` ~912). `env` is `none` for a fork-PR Run locked out of\n  secrets, and for a step before its Environment approval or after the approval went stale.\n- Claims include `run_id`, `attempt`, `git_ref`; `event` is hard-coded `\"deploy\"` and `sha` is\n  empty (`secret_executor.rs` ~724-734).\n\n\n1. **Only steps in a Run bound to an Environment get a token.** `mint_oidc_token` returns none\n   when the step has no `DeployContext` (`secret_executor.rs` ~703). Treebo's tofu-plan and\n   image-push steps may not run under an `environment:`, so they would get no token as things\n   stand. Decide whether a token without an Environment should exist (e.g. `env/none`) and\n   what AWS may trust it for.\n2. **AWS must fetch discovery and JWKS over the public internet.** Treebo's Scarab UI\n   host is private, and the only public route serves just the GitHub webhook path. Options:\n   - expose only `/.well-known/*` publicly;\n   - publish a static discovery doc and JWKS somewhere public (e.g. S3) and set the issuer URL\n     there. The issuer URL must equal the discovery location's origin, so this decides\n     `SCARAB_OIDC_ISSUER`.\n3. **The AWS SDK needs `AWS_ROLE_ARN` and `AWS_WEB_IDENTITY_TOKEN_FILE`.** Nothing in Scarab\n   sets them for a step today (only scarab-storage-s3 reads them, for Scarab's own access).\n   Should a step say which role it wants and Scarab set both variables, or do step authors set\n   them? The existing ECR docs touch this: `ui/scarab-docs-ui/src/content/docs/usage/pushing-to-ecr.mdx`.\n4. **The audience is one value for the whole server.** AWS IAM OIDC providers list allowed\n   client IDs; check whether one audience is enough or whether per-cloud audiences are needed.\n5. **Key rotation**: a single PEM, no rotation story found; the JWKS publishes one key.\n6. **`event` and `sha`** claims are fixed or empty; trust policies could want the real event\n   (push, pull_request, manual) or the commit.\n7. **The IRSA roles are still mounted.** Moving to OIDC means removing the broad roles from\n   the `scarab-steps` ServiceAccounts, or AWS still grants them to every step.\n\n\nStep Pods on the tools cluster that need AWS:\n- devops-gitops tofu-plan: assume the read-only Terraform plan role in each environment account;\n- image pushes to the root account's ECR (de-tools, woodpecker/ci-tools, agent-data-gateway-mcp);\n- dwh bootstrap (planned): read one SSM parameter in the staging and production accounts. This is\n  where a narrow role was first proposed and parked.\n\nThe verbs are AWS ones (assume role, ECR push, SSM read), not Scarab API calls. People and\nagents call the Scarab API with person-owned `scarab_pat_` tokens; nothing at Treebo needs a\nnon-person Scarab principal today. AWS account IDs and hostnames are left out of this ticket.\n\n\nThe issuer is not enabled: `/.well-known/openid-configuration` returns 404 and no `SCARAB_OIDC_*`\nis set in devops-gitops `tools/scarab`. No issuer URL, audience, IAM provider, role or expiry has\nbeen chosen. The signing key would come from SSM through the existing `scarab-env` ExternalSecret.\n\n\n1. Confirm the reading above: this is outbound federation to AWS, not Scarab service accounts.\n2. Gap 1: should steps outside an Environment get a token, and with what subject?\n3. Gap 2: public `/.well-known/*` route, or static discovery published to S3?\n4. Gap 3: should Scarab set the role ARN and token-file env for a step, and from what (a step\n   field, an Environment setting, a library input)?\n5. Where the devops-gitops side is tracked (a plan in that repo was offered); Scarab-side changes would want their own ADR or an amendment to ADR-0015\n   (ADRs are only edited when the owner asks).","files":null}]}